That's obvious part, yes.  The usual approach then involves a
controlled teleport *next to* the bad guy.  Eventually he'll vacate
the stairs so you can claim them.  Most serial ascenders use a variant
of this method.

The non-obvious part of "the blind teleport trick" centers around the
controlled teleport to a specific location in blank, unmapped space.
A location that, once the teleporting monster comes back to you, is
not marked in any way.  I typically do this several times during an
ascension.   I haven't seen anyone else attempt it, and thought I'd
share.

As Shawn Moore (aka Eidolos) pointed out upthread, all of these tricks
(in varying forms) have probably been discovered by several players.

